        "text": "We test our approach on the DomainBed benchmark (Gulrajani & Lopez-Paz, 2021), including: PACS (Li et al., 2017), VLCS (Fang et al., 2013), OfficeHome (Venkateswara et al., 2017), TerraIncognita (Beery et al., 2018), and DomainNet (Peng et al., 2019). For each dataset, we adopt the standard leave-one-domain-out source/target domain splits. The overall training/test protocols are similar to (Gulrajani & Lopez-Paz, 2021; Cha et al., 2021). We use the ResNet-50 (He et al., 2016) as our feature extractor backbone, which is initialized by the pretrained weights on ImageNet (Deng et al., 2009). For the generator network, we found that a linear model performed the best for the noise dimension 100. Our model is trained by the Adam optimizer (Kingma & Ba, 2015) on machines with single Tesla V100 GPUs. The hyperparameters introduced in our model (e.g., SMCD trade-off \u03b7) and the general ones (e.g., learning rate, SWAD regime hyperparameters, maximum numbers of iterations) are chosen by grid search on the validation set according to the DomainBed protocol (Gulrajani & Lopez-Paz, 2021). For instance, \u03b7 = 0.1 for all datasets. The implementation details including chosen hyperparameters can be found in Appendix A.1."
